{"step_index":973,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T03:00:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T22:00:51-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T22:00:51-05:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/gta%206%20mission%20workflow%20charts/gta6_mission_flow_chart.md`\nTotal Lines: 401\nTotal Bytes: 27080\nShowing lines 1 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Grand Theft Auto VI: Campaign Mission Flow & Prerequisite Guide\n2: \n3: This document provides the definitive mission dependency graph, prerequisite unlock trees, character-switching milestones, heist setup pipelines, points of no return, and speedrun routing across all 5 story chapters of *Grand Theft Auto VI*.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 1. High-Level Campaign Architecture\n8: \n9: The GTA VI storyline progresses through five distinct geographical and thematic narrative blocks. While open-world exploration is available between operations, missions operate in a strict Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) with key narrative bottlenecks connecting each chapter.\n10: \n11: ```mermaid\n12: flowchart TD\n13:     subgraph C1B[\"Prologue & Chapter 1\"]\n14:         C1[\"Just Like Paradise<br/>(Leonida Keys & Key Lento)<br/>Missions 1 - 18\"]\n15:     end\n16: \n17:     subgraph C2B[\"Chapter 2\"]\n18:         C2[\"Paradise Lost<br/>(Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)<br/>Missions 23 - 44\"]\n19:     end\n20: \n21:     subgraph C3B[\"Chapter 3\"]\n22:         C3[\"Vice City Syndicate Expansion<br/>(Vice City Metro & Sinfrontera Heist)<br/>Missions 45 - 70\"]\n23:     end\n24: \n25:     subgraph C4B[\"Chapter 4\"]\n26:         C4[\"Vice City Metro & Airport Takedown<br/>(Ocean Beach & VCIA Cargo Heist)<br/>Missions 71 - 95\"]\n27:     end\n28: \n29:     subgraph C5B[\"Chapter 5\"]\n30:         C5[\"Top of the World, Ma!<br/>(Climax, Standoff & Branching Endings)<br/>Missions 96 - 102\"]\n31:     end\n32: \n33:     C1 -->|\"Bottleneck: Doin' Gone\"| C2\n34:     C2 -->|\"Bottleneck: Checking Out\"| C3\n35:     C3 -->|\"Bottleneck: The Cartel Heist\"| C4\n36:     C4 -->|\"Point of No Return: Sunset\"| C5\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 2. Chapter 1: Just Like Paradise (Leonida Keys)\n42: \n43: ### Mechanics & Structure\n44: - **Playable Character**: Strictly locked to **Jason** (with Lucia introduced in the Prologue and reunited in *\"Coming Home\"*).\n45: - **Core Narrative**: Petty smuggling, local debt enforcement for Brian, and settling in Key Lento following Lucia's release from Hamlet State Penitentiary.\n46: - **True 3-Branch Parallel Architecture**: After completing *\"Gone Fishing\"* ($140 mailbox cash pickup), the storyline opens into three concurrent operational tracks:\n47:   1. **Branch 1 (Cal & Brian Marina Jobs)**: *Unwanted Attention* ($200 mailbox cash pickup) $\\rightarrow$ *Pipework*.\n48:   2. **Branch 2 (Brian Armory & Vehicle Repair)**: *Gear Up* $\\rightarrow$ *Just a Scratch* (Ganado repair & respray; **Mandatory Story Gate**).\n49:   3. **Branch 3 (Rent Collection & Main Spine)**: *Lab Fees* $\\rightarrow$ *Hey Arnold!* $\\rightarrow$ *Feng Shui* (24h cooldown wait) $\\rightarrow$ *Coming Home* (Lucia released from prison) $\\rightarrow$ *Find Donnie's Package*.\n50: - **Decision Diamond 1 (Gate Check)**: Evaluates whether the player has completed *Just a Scratch*. If not completed, Joey places an urgent reminder call redirecting Jason back to clear the repair shop gate before *Buck Me* unlocks.\n51: - **Decision Diamond 2 (Smuggler Gate Check)**: Evaluates whether BOTH *Day Release* AND *Just a Scratch* are completed before Brian's call triggers *Swamped*.\n52: - **Chapter 1 Climax**: *Swamped* $\\rightarrow$ *Doin' Gone* (clearing Donnie's trailer). The chapter cleanly terminates here with a hard narrative cut to Port Gellhorn.\n53: - **Speedrun Routing Note**: Clear Branch 1 (*Unwanted Attention* & *Pipework*) during the mandatory 24-hour waiting window triggered after *Feng Shui* to eliminate downtime. Skip all optional relationship/heart tasks (*Buy Necklace*, *Buy Flowers*, *Buy Groceries*, *Lucia's Clothes*).\n54: \n55: ```mermaid\n56: flowchart TD\n57:     M01[\"1. Prologue<br/>(Lucia Prison Counselor Interview)\"] --> M02[\"2. Gone Fishing<br/>(Jason & Donnie Boat Drop - $140 Mailbox)\"]\n58:     \n59:     %% Split Bar into 3 Tracks\n60:     M02 --> B1_Split[\"3-Track Branch Split\"]\n61:     \n62:     subgraph Track1[\"Branch 1: Cal & Marina Odd Jobs\"]\n63:         M06[\"6. Unwanted Attention<br/>(Cal Hamlet Trip - $200 Mailbox)\"] --> M07[\"7. Pipework<br/>(Marina Maintenance Jobs)\"]\n64:     end\n65:     \n66:     subgraph Track2[\"Branch 2: Brian Armory & Gate\"]\n67:         M03[\"3. Gear Up<br/>(Longarm Pickup)\"] --> M04[\"4. Just a Scratch<br/>(Ganado Respray - MANDATORY GATE)\"]\n68:     end\n69:     \n70:     subgraph Track3[\"Branch 3: Main Narrative Spine\"]\n71:         M05[\"5. Lab Fees<br/>(Rent Collection)\"] --> M08[\"8. Hey Arnold!<br/>(Cargo Broker Recon)\"]\n72:         M08 -.-> M09[\"9. Island Dreams<br/>(Optional Keys Diving)\"]\n73:         M08 --> M10[\"10. Feng Shui<br/>(Move Furniture - 24h Cooldown)\"]\n74:         M10 --> M11[\"11. Coming Home<br/>★ LUCIA RELEASED FROM PRISON ★\"]\n75:         M11 --> M12[\"12. Find Donnie's Package<br/>(Hamlet Retrieval)\"]\n76:     end\n77:     \n78:     B1_Split --> M06\n79:     B1_Split --> M03\n80:     B1_Split --> M05\n81:     \n82:     %% Decision Diamond 1\n83:     M12 --> DIA1{\"Did player finish<br/>JUST A SCRATCH?\"}\n84:     DIA1 -->|\"NO\"| JOEY[\"Joey Reminder Call<br/>(Redirects to Just a Scratch)\"]\n85:     JOEY -.-> M04\n86:     M04 -.-> DIA1\n87:     \n88:     DIA1 -->|\"YES\"| M13[\"13. Buck Me<br/>(Banking App Setup & Deposit)\"]\n89:     M13 --> M14[\"14. Down to Earth<br/>(Marina Smuggling Run - $600 Mailbox)\"]\n90:     M14 --> M15[\"15. Clear Skies<br/>(Southwind Bikers)\"]\n91:     M15 --> M16[\"16. Day Release<br/>(Rusty Anchor Bar Night Out)\"]\n92:     \n93:     %% Decision Diamond 2\n94:     M16 --> DIA2{\"Are DAY RELEASE &<br/>JUST A SCRATCH both done?\"}\n95:     M04 ==>|\"Mandatory Check\"| DIA2\n96:     \n97:     DIA2 -->|\"YES\"| M17[\"17. Swamped<br/>(Kingfishers Smugglers Meet)\"]\n98:     M17 --> M18[\"18. Doin' Gone<br/>★ CHAPTER 1 CLIMAX ★<br/>(Clear Donnie's Trailer)\"]\n99:     \n100:     M18 -->|\"Hard Transition\"| C2_Start[\"→ Chapter 2: What's in the Bag?<br/>(Starlet Motel Arrival)\"]\n101: ```\n102: \n103: ---\n104: \n105: ## 3. Chapter 2: Paradise Lost (Port Gellhorn & Kelly County)\n106: \n107: ### Mechanics & Structure\n108: - **Playable Character**: Heavily centered on **Lucia** during early recovery, then **permanently unlocks Dual Character Switching** via *\"Coffee Break\"*.\n109: - **Vehicle Fencing**: Unlocked via *\"Moses\"* (enabling Slim Jim vehicle thefts and custom garage registrations).\n110: - **Strict Chronological Sequence**: Unlike Chapter 3, Chapter 2 is organized into **4 sequential stages** that must be cleared in order (M23 through M44).\n111:   - **Stage 1: Motel Arrival & Medical (M23–M28)**: Infiltration, paying upkeep, Lucia solo medical run, and establishing fencing with Moses.\n112:   - **Stage 2: Debt Hustle & Gun Runs (M29–M37)**: Disguise setups, ambulance chasing, painkiller supply lines, and corner meetups.\n113:   - **Stage 3: Dual Character Switching & Robberies (M38–M40)**: *Coffee Break* unlocks instant partner switching; *Hit Avery Pawn* introduces business robberies.\n114:   - **Stage 4: Highway Escape & Move to Vice City (M41–M44)**: Vehicle recovery, Kelly County smugglers, and the motel evacuation climax in *Checking Out*.\n115: \n116: ```mermaid\n117: flowchart TD\n118:     C1_Trans[\"From Ch. 1: Doin' Gone\"] --> S1_Start\n119:     \n120:     subgraph S1[\"Stage 1: Motel Arr