ach** | 70. The Cartel Heist | Establishes Y Hotel safehouse | Fast oceanfront spawn point |\n362: | **Ch. 4** | **75. Party Hard** | 74. Lawyer Up | Corrupt lawyer Abe Gonzalez legal immunity | **$75k BuckMe wire gate** (instant pass if cash saved) |\n363: | **Ch. 4** | **88. Headliners** | 87. Child's Play | Dre'Quan concert finale; unlocks airport recon | Concludes Dre'Quan alliance arc |\n364: | **Ch. 4** | **93. VCIA Takedown** | 92. Fully Catered | **Major Airport Cargo Heist** | Awards *Hi-Jacked* trophy |\n365: | **Ch. 4** | **94. Sunset** | 93. VCIA Takedown | **POINT OF NO RETURN** | Locks open-world roaming and manual saves |\n366: | **Ch. 4** | **95. Starting From Zero** | 94. Sunset | Chapter 4 climax evacuation | Immediate continuation into Chapter 5 |\n367: | **Ch. 5** | **99. Two Hundred Percent** | 98. Scorched Earth | Assault on Mendez compound | High-intensity tactical combat gauntlet |\n368: | **Ch. 5** | **100. Standoff Decision** | 99. Two Hundred Percent| Key West Motel ambush by Mendez | Choose Ending A, B, or C |\n369: | **Ch. 5** | **Ending B: The Deal** | 100. Standoff (Immunity)| Partner accepts federal plea | **FASTEST ANY% ROUTE (Saves 8–12 minutes)** |\n370: | **Ch. 5** | **Ending A: Bonnie & Clyde** | 100. Standoff (Loyalty) | Partner trust; offshore Coast Guard battle | **Awards $2,000,000 cash payout** (Not a gate!) |\n371: | **Ch. 5** | **101–102. Epilogue & Credits**| Any Ending Selected | Campaign concluded; free roam restored | Full Leonida map unlocked for post-game |\n372: \n373: ---\n374: \n375: ## 8. Fact-Checking & Ground Truth Discrepancy Analysis\n376: \n377: ### 1. Verified Reference Data (`image_1188e9.jpg`) vs. Speculative Community Outlines\n378: Early community diagrams circulating online contained several critical errors and speculative extrapolations:\n379: 1. **Chapter 1 Climax is *Doin' Gone* (Not Speculative Missions 19–22)**:\n380:    - The community flowchart `GTAVI_MISSION_FLOW1.jpg` mistakenly spelled this mission as `\"DON GONE\"`. Cross-referencing verified game strings and audio logs confirms the title is **\"Doin' Gone\"** (referencing Donnie's departure and cleaning out his trailer).\n381:    - In speculative outlines, missions 19–22 (*Recalibration*, *Tourist Trap*, *Home Sweet Home*, *Discharge Time*) were extrapolated as Chapter 1 missions. Ground truth reference `image_1188e9.jpg` clearly terminates Chapter 1 at *Doin' Gone*, routing directly into the Port Gellhorn motel arrival (*What's in the Bag?*).\n382: 2. **True 3-Branch Parallel Structure**:\n383:    - The storyline splits immediately after *Gone Fishing* into 3 concurrent branches (*Unwanted Attention*, *Gear Up*, *Lab Fees*). Forcing missions 1 to 22 into a linear chain misrepresents the game's actual Directed Acyclic Graph.\n384: 3. **The Two Explicit Decision Diamonds**:\n385:    - **Diamond 1**: Evaluates whether *Just a Scratch* has been cleared prior to *Buck Me*. If skipped, an automated call from Joey intercepts progression.\n386:    - **Diamond 2**: Evaluates whether both *Day Release* and *Just a Scratch* are completed before *Swamped* $\\rightarrow$ *Doin' Gone*.\n387: \n388: ### 2. The Ending A $2,000,000 Payout Clarification\n389: - A common misconception in player communities is that Ending A (*Bonnie & Clyde*) requires $2,000,000 in the player's bank account to unlock.\n390: - **Fact**: Script analysis confirms that **$2,000,000 is the mission completion cash reward** paid out to Jason and Lucia upon successfully surviving the Coast Guard gauntlet, NOT an entry prerequisite. Players do not need to grind money before initiating the finale.\n391: \n392: ### 3. Strict Sequential Progression vs. Concurrent Parallel Strands\n393: - **Chapters 2 & 4 (Sequential Stages)**: Visual \"wrap-around\" diagonal arrows in older community flowcharts made Chapters 2 and 4 look like parallel faction branches. In reality, they are strict chronological stages (Stages 1 through 4) where each phase must be fully cleared before the next stage opens.\n394: - **Chapter 3 (True Parallel Faction Strands)**: Once the Vice City safehouse is unlocked in Mission 50, Tyrone (Strand 1), Boobie (Strand 2), and Raul (Strand 3) are active simultaneously as concurrent map pins. Furthermore, the Sinfrontera Bank Heist features 3 concurrent preparation tracks (Safecracker, Explosives, Codes & Van) that can be tackled in any order.\n395: \n396: ### 4. Any% Speedrun Optimization Summary\n397: - **Chapter 1 Downtime Optimization**: Run Branch 1 (*Unwanted Attention* $\\rightarrow$ *Pipework*) while *Feng Shui*'s 24-hour waiting window elapses.\n398: - **Skip All Social / Hot Meter Activities**: Ignore *Get Haircut*, *Buy Necklace*, *Buy Flowers*, *Buy Groceries*, and *Lucia's Clothes*.\n399: - **Save $75,000 Cash**: Keep at least $75,000 from the Sinfrontera Bank Heist ($10.5M take) to instantly bypass Abe Gonzalez's wire transfer gate in Chapter 4 (*Party Hard*).\n400: - **Select Ending B (*The Deal*)**: Accepting Mendez's immunity plea skips the multi-stage offshore Coast Guard gunboat battle, saving **8 to 12 minutes of real-world time** in Any% speedruns.\n401: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
